  "scope": "# Review: generator `90640e0e6314`\nTask/source: production version `3.0.0`, generator SHA-256 `97508cbdd531c0ba6b564aaf818b6a58adf829abfdaaaab45b89e97f176a401e`, rule hash `370706e398d4`.\nAssignment: `review-0194f3df79424525`; parametric priority for original ARC family `training:833dafe3`.\nMissing deliverable \u2192 repair: built a task-local, finite `identity_corner` parameter prototype plus exact Racket verifier and public/private artifact writer.\nPrototype settings: `top_left`, `top_right`, `bottom_left`, `bottom_right`; the original `bottom_right` setting is the exact canonical default and is fixed once per episode.\nEpisode counts: demonstrations and queries are independent positive controls, each bounded to `1..64`; the retained default is 3 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries.\nProduction generator and canonical authority: unchanged; no approval, catalog selection, runtime integration, or training admission is claimed.\nVerification: isolated staged task suite passes **16/16** after a portable canonical-data test repair; the pre-fix staged failure is retained.\nRacket evidence: **4 episodes \u00d7 7 shared inputs = 28 setting calls**, plus all **3** labeled canonical pairs; all exact, all four labels distinct, and every 3-demo lesson refutes every query-changing rival across 4 queries.\nPublic projection: IDs derive only from exact visible bytes; hidden setting, seed, programs, and answers remain private; duplicate visible payloads and overwrite collisions are rejected.\nSupplementary tickets: pinned audit witness reproduced without clearing the audit; bounded allocation probe completed on a deterministic 3/300 sample and proposes a measured 40-assignment A/B test.\nDisposition: routine prototype/test improvement; maintainer attention is needed only before adoption because the finite family remains proposed and non-admitted.",
